 "90b4534a-4d56-520e-9cbd-ca4ad433ac7c" 13194139536200 true] [17592186388611 1034 "-\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139536200 true] [17592186388611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536200 true] [17592186388611 1111 #uuid "9b703e0c-1828-55e5-be16-9b8fa50851e8" 13194139536200 true] [17592186388612 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388613 13194139536200 true] [17592186388612 1089 "q-278290" 13194139536200 true] [17592186388612 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536200 true] [17592186388612 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/36aeda6b6f5ce46552f55f458da60ef46a646d737c452d586389c03c47d1c9cb.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g$ and $P$ divides $\\overset{―}{FG}$ in the ratio $FP:PG=8:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OP}.$" 13194139536200 true] [17592186388612 1113 #uuid "cb79b649-cc96-59ab-927e-8bb7778fa82d" 13194139536200 true] [17592186388612 1145 "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{FP}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OFG,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =\\overset{\\to }{FO}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-f+g \\\\  & =g-f.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $FP:PG=8:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{FP}=\\frac{8}{13}\\overset{\\to }{FG}=\\frac{8}{13}(g-f).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP} \\\\  & =f+\\frac{8}{13}(g-f) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}f+\\frac{8}{13}g.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536200 true] [17592186388613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388614 13194139536200 true] [17592186388613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388615 13194139536200 true] [17592186388613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388616 13194139536200 true] [17592186388613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388617 13194139536200 true] [17592186388613 1000 #edb/ref 1759